@startuml class-boundary-control
title Class Diagram (3/3) - Boundary and Control Integration\nHow the UI, controllers, services, and external interfaces connect to the domain

top to bottom direction
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontSize 12
skinparam packageFontSize 13
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 130
hide empty members
hide circle

package "Boundary" #FAFAFA {
  interface ReservationUI
  class SwingApp
  interface PaymentGatewayInterface
  interface SkypassInterface
  interface GDSInterface
  class MockSkypassInterface #FFE0E0

  ReservationUI <|.. SwingApp
  SkypassInterface <|.. MockSkypassInterface
}

package "Control - Services and orchestration" #FAFAFA {
  class BookingController
  class AuthService
  class PaymentProcessor #FFD0D0
  class RefundHandler
  class FlightSearchService
  class ReservationLookupService
  class ItinerarySearchService #FFE0E0
  class SeatHoldMonitor #FFE0E0
  class TicketPurchasePublisher #FFE0E0
  class ReservationRegistry #FFE0E0
}

class "Reservation" as Reservation #FFD0D0
class "Itinerary" as Itinerary #FFD0D0
class "RefundPolicy" as RefundPolicy <<interface>>

SwingApp --> BookingController
SwingApp --> AuthService
SwingApp --> ReservationLookupService

BookingController --> Reservation
BookingController --> PaymentProcessor
BookingController --> SeatHoldMonitor
BookingController --> ItinerarySearchService

PaymentProcessor --> PaymentGatewayInterface
PaymentProcessor --> MockSkypassInterface
ItinerarySearchService --> FlightSearchService
RefundHandler --> RefundPolicy
ReservationRegistry o-- "*" Reservation

note bottom of MockSkypassInterface
  Iter3 boundary class.
  Real Skypass HTTP API
  integration is post-course.
end note

note right of ItinerarySearchService
  Iter3 service. Walks the
  flight catalog and validates
  connecting itineraries
  against the MCT.
end note
@enduml
